# CLI deploys are launched from the REPO ROOT: the project's Root Directory
# setting (`api`) then points the build at `api/` inside this uploaded tree —
# which is also how `../frontend` becomes visible to `api/scripts/vercel-build.sh`.
#
# So this file must NOT blank the tree (that broke the build). It only keeps
# secrets and local state off the wire. Plain `.env` is here because Vercel's
# built-in ignore list covers only `.env.local` / `.env.*.local`.
.env
.env.*
*.local
node_modules
.vercel
.vercel/*
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
